&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help make the world more hospitable &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The hospitality industry is uniquely human, and it deserves technology that’s just as inspiring as the people behind it. At Mews, we’re transforming the industry with a platform that helps hotels run smarter, move faster and create better guest experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work with smart, curious people who care deeply about what they do. You’ll have autonomy and the trust to make good decisions and move quickly. And you’ll enjoy a real sense of purpose as you see the impact of what we’re building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re motivated by ownership, curiosity and meaningful impact, and are driven to deliver consistent high performance, you’ll feel at home here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let&#39;s get into the specifics. It’s impossible to capture every nuance of a role – especially at a rapidly growing company like Mews – but if we had to distil it into a job description (which we do because this is a job description), it would be this:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;You&#39;d own the design and delivery of Mews&#39; first dedicated commercial enablement function inside Onboarding: turning onboarding professionals across a global, distributed team into consultants who can spot and act on expansion revenue, without inheriting anyone else&#39;s playbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most onboarding organisations treat go-live as the finish line, so the upsell and cross-sell signals sitting inside existing project portfolios go unqualified and never reach Sales. At Mews, that gap sits inside a fast-growing hospitality tech customer base, where every project portfolio onboarding already manages is effectively an unworked pipeline of expansion revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with Onboarding leadership globally, plus Sales, Customer Success and RevOps, to define what a qualified expansion lead looks like and get it moving to the right team. This is a new role, not a backfill, so the coaching model, playbooks and success metrics are yours to build from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role exists because Onboarding&#39;s project portfolios are growing faster than the team&#39;s ability to work them commercially, and right now, nobody owns that motion end to end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you would do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver consultative sales training for onboarding professionals, covering discovery, opportunity qualification, objection handling and commercial conversations that keep the customer&#39;s trust intact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an ongoing coaching programme that grows consultative skill progressively, from new joiners through tenured consultants, and onboard new starters into the commercial side of the role from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop playbooks and frameworks, including AI-assisted tools, that help the team surface and qualify upsell and cross-sell signals across their project portfolios at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Customer Success and RevOps to define a qualified expansion lead and build the handoff process between Onboarding and Sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track commercial performance across the portfolio (pipeline generated, expansion revenue influenced, handoff quality) and use it to keep improving the programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Fluency Level 3:&lt;/strong&gt; in this role, that means redesigning how the wider onboarding team spots and qualifies commercial signals, not just using AI to work faster yourself. You&#39;ll build AI-assisted frameworks and tools that other onboarding professionals can use on their own portfolios, and you&#39;ll actively check what those tools flag before it shapes a playbook or gets treated as a qualified lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For more information on AI fluency at Mews, please refer to &lt;a href=&quot;https://mews.atlassian.net/wiki/x/XQOskg&quot;&gt;&quot;AI Fluency at Mews: A Comprehensive Guide for Candidates&quot;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you would bring&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years in Revenue Enablement, Sales Enablement or Commercial Training, with direct exposure to consultative or solution-selling methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background as a quota-carrying sales rep, account manager or customer success leader: you&#39;ve had the commercial conversations you&#39;ll be teaching others to have&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with consultative sales frameworks (MEDDPICC, Challenger, SPIN or equivalent), and comfort adapting them to a post-sale, trust-based context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A coaching instinct: you can watch a customer interaction, spot the missed commercial moment, and give feedback specific enough to change what happens next time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI Fluency Level 3 or equivalent hands-on experience: comfortable redesigning workflows with AI, building tools colleagues can reuse, and checking AI output rather than taking it at face value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-driven mindset: comfortable defining success metrics and iterating a programme based on results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and delivering training for customer-facing teams in a SaaS B2B environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong facilitation and presentation skills, and comfort operating across a large, distributed global team where influence often has to happen without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
